* text=auto eol=lf
*.snk binary
*.png binary
*.bmp binary
*.tif binary
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
*.odt binary
*.ttf binary
# An email fixture keeps its CRLF line ends, as the MIME it is; a .msg is a compound file.
*.eml binary
*.msg binary
*.pdf binary

*.verified.txt text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.verified.xml text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.verified.json text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.verified.html text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.verified.md text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

src/.editorconfig text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.sln.DotSettings text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
*.slnx.DotSettings text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8

*NonStandardEncoding* binary
